---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="About Kilnbook"
	description="Kilnbook was started in 2022 by a studio owner and a software engineer in Portland, Oregon, to replace the kiln log clipboard."
>
	<section class="band-dark page-hero">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">About Kilnbook</p>
				<h1>We started with a clipboard on a kiln.</h1>
			<p>
				In 2022 Maren Østby was running Clay Collective PDX, a 14-wheel community studio on SE
				Division Street. Every firing was tracked on a clipboard taped to the kiln room door, and every
				month ended with her matching that clipboard to a pile of Venmo payments.
			</p>
			<p>
				Theo Achebe was one of her members, and a backend engineer. He built a small app so members
				could log their pieces from a phone. Within a year three other Portland studios were asking to
				use it, and Kilnbook became a company.
			</p>
		</div>
			<img
				src="/images/studio-floor.svg"
				alt="Illustrated overhead view of a pottery studio floor with six wheels, a kiln room, shelves of drying pieces and a glaze table"
				width="560"
				height="360"
			/>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-alt">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2>What we believe</h2>
			<div class="cards">
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Studios are not gyms</h3>
					<p>
						Generic booking tools do not know what a bisque load is. We build for the way clay
						actually moves through a studio.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Members should see the queue</h3>
					<p>
						Half the questions at a studio front desk are "is my bowl out yet?" Kilnbook answers that
						one before anyone has to ask.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Small team, real support</h3>
					<p>
						We are nine people. Four of us throw every week, and support is answered by people who
						have loaded a kiln.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>The team</h2>
		<p>
			Kilnbook is based in Portland, Oregon, with teammates in Asheville and Leeds. We are
			bootstrapped and profitable, and we plan to stay that way.
		</p>
		<p>
			Want to work with us? We are not hiring right now, but we always read notes from potters who
			write code. <a href="/contact">Say hello</a>.
		</p>
	</section>
</Base>
